// Western: original stories written for this game. Format: docs/v3/BLUEPRINT-FORMAT.md.

== western.f01 | feature | three-act
title: The Well At Dry Fork
genre: western + drama
tone: Spare, sun-struck and stubborn, with dry humour between hard choices
era: 1887 | period
setting: Dry Fork, New Mexico Territory | fictional | desert
logline: A widowed well-digger hired to find water for a dying town strikes it on the one claim she cannot legally touch, and has four days before the railroad's surveyor decides whether the town is worth a station.
premise: {marta} digs wells for a living and is paid only when the water comes. Dry Fork has had none for two summers and has pooled its last money to hire her. Her rod and her reading of the rock both say the water is under the abandoned Kessler claim, which the bank's man {pruitt} is holding for a buyer back East.
synopsis: {marta} arrives in Dry Fork with a mule, a rig and a reputation the town can barely afford. She walks the ground for a day and tells the council what they do not want to hear: every hole they have dug is on the wrong side of a fault, and the water is under the Kessler claim. {pruitt}, who holds the paper on half the town, refuses to let her dig there. The schoolteacher {eli} finds in the county ledger that the claim lapses if nobody works it for a year and a day, which falls in four days, the same morning the railroad's surveyor {hask} rides out. {marta} digs a decoy on town land by day and, with {eli} and the blacksmith's daughter {june}, sinks the true shaft on the Kessler side by night. {pruitt} learns of it and offers {marta} three times her fee to hit rock and leave. She takes his money in front of the town, and loses its trust. On the last night the shaft floods early and traps {june}; {marta} goes down after her and {pruitt}, who has followed to catch them trespassing, has to choose whether to haul the rope. He hauls. At sunrise the claim has lapsed, the water is standing in the shaft, and {marta} lays {pruitt}'s money on the council table as the filing fee for a town well. {hask} marks Dry Fork for a station. {marta} is paid, and leaves before the celebrating starts.
question: Will {marta} do the job she was hired for when the law, the money and her own rule about staying out of a town's quarrels all tell her to leave?
themes: who owns what is under the ground; a stranger's honesty against a neighbour's; work as a kind of faith
audience: Adults and older teenagers who like a western about work and law more than gunfights
viewpoint: With {marta}, an outsider reading a town the way she reads rock
stakes: Without water the railroad passes Dry Fork by and forty families walk away from everything they own; {marta} loses the only thing she trades on, her word
conflict: A town's need against a paper right, and {marta}'s rule of never taking sides against her need to finish what she starts
ending: The claim lapses with water in the shaft. {marta} pays the filing fee with {pruitt}'s bribe, collects her wage and rides out alone while the town drinks.
experience: Thirst you can feel, the slow satisfaction of a hole going down, and a final morning that arrives like rain
look: White noon that flattens everything, then lamplight in a narrow shaft; the only green in the picture is the last shot
sound: Wind, a windlass creaking, the changing note of a pick as rock turns to damp clay. A single fiddle, late.
m: find | institution | self-vs-others | triumph
@ marta | Marta Oyelaran-Reyes | lead | protagonist | human | she/her | 44 | To bring in the well and be gone | A dry hole in Socorro cost her husband his life and her name | The water is under ground she has no right to break | Trusts rock more than people and is rarely wrong about either | From hired hand to someone who takes a side | Plain, exact, counts things aloud | Weathered, rope-scarred hands, a man's coat cut down
@ eli | Eli Castellanos | supporting | ally | human | he/him | 31 | To keep the school open one more year | It is the only thing he has built | He believes the law is fair if you read it closely | A rule-keeper who finds the loophole | From reading the law to using it | Careful, bookish, apologises before disagreeing | Thin, ink on his cuffs, spectacles mended with wire
@ june | June Abernathy | supporting | ally | human | she/her | 17 | To learn a trade that takes her out of Dry Fork | Her father expects her to keep his books | She is not supposed to be down a shaft at all | Fearless underground, shy above it | From helper to digger | Quick questions, then silence while she works | Strong shoulders, a burn scar on one forearm
@ pruitt | Silas Pruitt | supporting | antagonist | human | he/him | 55 | To deliver the Kessler claim clean to his buyer | It is his own way out of the territory | He likes these people and holds their debts | Courteous, fair by his own lights, and for sale | From owning the town to belonging to it | Soft-spoken, uses first names like receipts | Neat grey suit gone white with dust
@ hask | Lieutenant Wren Hask | featured | none | human | he/him | 38 | To file an honest survey and go home | He has seen three towns die on his reports | Nobody tells him the truth because of what he decides | Kind, and powerless to be kind officially | Unchanged, but relieved | Clipped, numerical | Army bearing, sunburnt neck, a level in a leather case
~ marta - pruitt | hired digger and the man holding the paper | polite enemies who respect each other's competence | he hauls her rope, and she spends his bribe on the town
~ marta - june | digger and unasked-for apprentice | {marta} wants no helper | she leaves {june} her second-best pick
~ marta - eli | outsider and the one local who backs her | he trusts the ledger, she trusts the rod | each has taken up a little of the other's method
~ pruitt - eli | creditor and debtor | {eli} owes for the schoolhouse stove | the debt is forgiven without either saying so
# Opening | EXT | Dry Fork, Main Street | DAY | marta, pruitt, eli | Bring the stranger in and price the job | {marta} waters her mule from her own barrel while the town watches; the council counts out a retainer in small coins and {pruitt} tops it up with a note | | 4 | animals=mule, props=water barrel+dowsing rod
# Opening | EXT | Kessler Claim | DUSK | marta, june | Find the water in the wrong place | The rod drops over a line of dead mesquite; {june}, following uninvited, shows her a seep stain on the claim marker | {marta} learns whose land it is | 4 | props=dowsing rod+claim marker
# Development | INT | Schoolhouse | NIGHT | marta, eli | Find the way through the law | {eli} reads the lapse clause aloud by a stove he has not paid for; they count the days on the slate | Four days, ending the morning the surveyor leaves | 3 | props=county ledger+slate
# Development | EXT | Town Lot Behind The Livery | DAY | marta, pruitt, hask | Dig the decoy in plain sight | {marta} sinks a dry hole while {hask} sets up his level and {pruitt} brings lemonade and an offer | She pockets his money where everyone can see | 5 | props=windlass+surveyor's level, crowd=20
# Escalation | INT | Kessler Shaft | NIGHT | marta, june, eli | Go down for real | Lantern, bucket and rope; the pick's note changes and the clay comes up dark. {eli} hauls badly and learns | | 6 | props=lantern+pick+rope
# Escalation | EXT | Main Street | DAY | marta, eli, pruitt | Lose the town | Word of the bribe is out. Nobody will sell her feed. {eli} asks her straight and she will not explain with {pruitt} listening | {eli} keeps digging anyway | 3 | crowd=25
# Climax | INT | Kessler Shaft | NIGHT | marta, june, pruitt | Flood and rescue | The floor gives way to water with {june} at the bottom; {marta} goes down the rope, and {pruitt}, arriving to catch trespassers, is the only one at the windlass | He hauls them both up | 7 | water, stunts=shaft flood and rope haul, props=windlass+rope
# Resolution | INT | Council Room Over The Store | DAWN | marta, pruitt, eli, hask | Make it legal | The lapse hour passes on {eli}'s watch. {marta} counts {pruitt}'s bribe onto the table as the filing fee; {hask} marks his map | {pruitt} signs as witness | 4 | props=pocket watch+survey map
# Resolution | EXT | Road Out Of Dry Fork | DAY | marta, june | Pay and part | The town drinks behind her. {june} runs up with the wage the council forgot; {marta} hands down the second-best pick | | 3 | animals=mule, crowd=40
